<title>ISRAEL: Telrad to buy shares in parent Koor.</title>
<headline>Telrad to buy shares in parent Koor.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telrad Holdings Ltd has decided to buy a further $10 million of shares in its parent company, Koor Industries Ltd, Israel's largest industrial concern.</p>
<p>Koor said in a letter to the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange on Wednesday that the purchase would be made on and off the floor. Earlier this month Telrad bought $4 million in Koor shares.</p>
<p>Telrad owns 71,344 shares in Koor, equal to 0.245 percent of the equity or 0.472 percent of the voting rights.</p>
<p>Israeli companies are prohibited by law from buying their own shares but subsidiaries may buy shares in parent companies.</p>
<p>($1=3.41 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom 972-3-5372211</p>
